Why: PentAGI's worker containers must go through cell-guard (DEVELOPMENT_PLAN §2.4),
and cell-guard refuses six things RunContainer and WorkerSpec ask for at b611fbe:
published ports (PortBindings), an on-failure restart policy, a json-file LogConfig, a
named /work volume bound by name, a Hostname without the cell's prefix, and added
capabilities beyond NET_RAW. This patch drops each of them:
  - no PortBindings/ExposedPorts: the worker is reached on its cell address instead;
  - no RestartPolicy and no LogConfig: the daemon's defaults apply ("no", rotation);
  - /work is an anonymous volume (HostConfig.Mounts), removed with the container;
  - no Hostname: the daemon uses the short container id;
  - capabilities: Docker's default set minus MKNOD with nothing added, which is
    PentAGI's own allow-list minus SYS_PTRACE (and minus NET_ADMIN, off by default).
Everything else in the request is unchanged. Touches backend/pkg/docker/client.go and
backend/pkg/docker/worker_spec.go.

